Sun Oct 18 17:38:20 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.9.1 (upstream tag v0.9.1, 2026-10-18):
  * Catalog: Lightroom import results fixed with lower CPU/memory use;
    DNG export writes the color the raw opens with; faces from replaced
    photos dropped.
  * Editing: Reset tooltip shows the platform shortcut; radial masks keep
    inside/outside from Lightroom; loupe overlay layout image; crop
    straighten/rotate and NaN-rect fixes; Show All Masks in zoom windows.
  * Never-crash fixes: raw size checks (PEF, TIFF tiles, ARW6), no
    write-through at temp-file links, CLI rejects non-object params.
  - Hardening: crafted Lightroom catalogs can no longer smuggle an
    executable into the library and run it via Open Original / Edit In;
    only file types LightCraft reads reach the system opener, and
    catalog paths are followed only on this computer or the catalog's
    share.
  * Packaging: HEIF images advertised, AppStream screenshot repaired.
  * Re-vendored (update=false kept for --locked, no in-tree vendor/ upstream;
    respect-lockfile true); license re-derived over shipped targets, no new
    copyleft (new crates all craft-family MIT/Apache-2.0), tag stands;
    no new system deps.

