Tue Oct 13 06:44:01 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.7.1 (includes 0.6.0, upstream tags v0.6.0 and v0.7.1):
  * HDR editing and export: gain map JPEG, PQ AVIF, float TIFF,
    16-bit Rec. 2020 PQ PNG, HDR histogram and HDR button in the
    Edit panel
  * New export options: JPEG XL, PSD, contact sheet PDF, Add to
    Apple Photos (macOS), watermark preview, all nine positions,
    separate insets and quarter-turn rotation
  * Edit in PhotoCraft (flat PSD hand-off)
  * Activity stack: one progress indicator for long-running tasks
  * Library: Keyword List and keywording box, folder colour
    labels, Synchronize Folder, creating folders on disk and moving
    photos, New Library and Open Recent Library, offline reverse
    geocoding, smart collection rules, Lightroom catalog detection
    when opening a library, Lightroom spot removal import
  * Develop: process versions, Lightroom-like Auto, content-aware
    Remove (PatchMatch), soft proofing against printer ICC
    profiles, Kelvin white balance for 52 camera models, Color
    Grading improvements, AI Denoise offload to another computer's
    graphics card, crop tool angle readout and Shift to keep
    proportions
  * Display: monitor ICC profiles, macOS previews follow the screen
    profile, system appearance and light themes, Lights Out view,
    sidebar sections, shared panel docking
  * Raw support: Sony ARW6 (ILCE-7RM6), DSC-R1 SR2, Fujifilm RAF
    and DNG WarpRectilinear2 lens corrections, Canon CR3 C-RAW
    fixes (EOS R5 Mark II, R50, R7), Nikon lossy and High
    Efficiency NEF handling, Olympus ORF, Hasselblad 3FR, Kodak
    DCS520C, DNG 1.7 and HEIC (release builds)
  * New translations: French, Ukrainian, Simplified Chinese;
    updated Russian
  * Linux riscv64 release build; Wayland file dialogs are children
    of the app window and XWayland is the default for drag-and-drop
  * Windows MSI: choose the install folder, and upgrades from older
    installers keep the legacy folder
  * Fixes for GPU denoise races, Intel Metal pipeline compile
    failures, library lock release on close, brush mask coverage,
    upper-case file extensions, and many UI behaviours
  * Full upstream notes:
    https://github.com/storytold/lightcraft/compare/v0.5.0...v0.7.1

