Sun Oct 11 06:59:11 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- New package lightcraft 0.5.0 (upstream tag v0.5.0, 2026-10-10),
  built from source with --features heif (pure-Rust heic-rs 0.1.1,
  no system HEIF library; HEVC patent comfort still open, disclosed
  in the Legal-Review-Notice).
- License derived over the vendor tree for the shipped targets
  (lightcraft, lightcraft-cli): no copyleft linked; tag covers the
  embedded OFL-1.1 Inter fonts, Ubuntu-font-1.0, IJG, Unicode-3.0,
  CC0-1.0, CDLA-Permissive-2.0 and Zlib/ISC/BSD/MIT permissive code,
  see the Legal-Review-Notice in the spec.
- Split off lightcraft-cli subpackage (headless renderer, command
  runner and MCP server); main package ships only the desktop app
  and recommends the CLI. License tag duplicated to the subpackage,
  Legal-Review-Notice still covers both targets incl. heif flag.
- Reorder Requires to spec-cleaner order (cosmetic).

